# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vriddhi — frontend environment template
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in the values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Every variable Vite exposes to the browser MUST be prefixed with `VITE_`.
# Without the prefix the value is silently undefined at runtime.
#
# All ten values below are consumed by the app:
#   * VITE_FIREBASE_*  -> src/Firebase/config.ts
#   * VITE_API_*       -> src/shared/api/apiBase.ts (the single normaliser used
#                         by the AI chat, AI question generation and PDF export
#                         clients)
#
# ⚠️  These are *public client-side* keys, not secrets. Anyone who loads the
#     deployed site can read them. Protect your data with Firestore /
#     Realtime Database security rules, not by hiding these values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Firebase web app config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where to find these:
#   Firebase console → your project → ⚙ Project settings → "Your apps"
#   → SDK setup and configuration → "Config"
# It is the object passed to initializeApp(), keys renamed with VITE_ prefixes.

# Required. Identifies the API key for the web app.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSy...your-api-key

# Required. Auth domain, normally <project-id>.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=vriddhi-engineering.firebaseapp.com

# Required. Realtime Database URL, normally
# https://<project-id>-default-rtdb.asia-south1.firebasedatabase.app
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://vriddhi-engineering-default-rtdb.asia-south1.firebasedatabase.app

# Required. The Firebase project ID.
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=vriddhi-engineering

# Required. Cloud Storage bucket, normally <project-id>.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=vriddhi-engineering.appspot.com

# Required. The numeric sender ID from the app config.
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123456789012

# Required. The app ID from the app config (format 1:<sender-id>:web:<hash>).
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456789012:web:abcdef0123456789

# Optional in Firebase itself, but read unconditionally by src/Firebase/config.ts.
# Leave blank only if Analytics is disabled for the project.
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Cloud Functions API base URL ────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is the preferred name; VITE_API_URL is accepted as a
# fallback. If neither is set, the code falls back to the production
# Functions URL in src/shared/api/apiBase.ts.
# Only one of the two is needed — set VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#
# The `/api` suffix is OPTIONAL: apiBase.ts appends it when missing and strips
# a trailing slash, so these are all equivalent:
#   https://asia-south1-vriddhi-engineering.cloudfunctions.net
#   https://asia-south1-vriddhi-engineering.cloudfunctions.net/api
#   https://asia-south1-vriddhi-engineering.cloudfunctions.net/api/
#
# Local development against the Functions emulator: set the value to `/api`
# and `npm run dev` proxies same-origin /api/* requests to
# http://localhost:5001/<VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID>/asia-south1/api
# (see vite.config.ts; override the target with VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET).

# Cloud Functions (regional endpoint, /api suffix included)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://asia-south1-vriddhi-engineering.cloudfunctions.net/api

# Item 4.4: the PDF routes (paper PDF, questions export, resume PDF) now run in
# their own `pdf` Cloud Function, because they launch headless Chrome and the
# ordinary API should not pay for a 2 GiB instance. Derived from
# VITE_API_BASE_URL by swapping the trailing `/api` for `/pdf`; set this only if
# the two functions ever live in different regions.
# VITE_PDF_BASE_URL=https://asia-south1-vriddhi-engineering.cloudfunctions.net/pdf

# Legacy alias. Safe to leave empty if VITE_API_BASE_URL is set.
VITE_API_URL=

# Dev only (optional): where the Vite proxy forwards /api/* when
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api. Defaults to the local Functions emulator.
# VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5001/vriddhi-engineering/asia-south1/api
